Overview

This document describes the process of adding new users to CymBuild.

Prerequisites

For a user to be able to login into the system, they first must be added to two SharePoint groups, namely CymBuild & Outlook. For this, please contact the IT department.

Even if not yet part of these groups, user details can still be added to CymBuild.

Adding a user

Users Section

The area from which a user can be added is in the settings area.  Once in there, locate the Users drawer item, then click the New button.

Figure 1 - Accessing The User Settings Area.

Entering User Details

Going from top to bottom, we have two sections: top half is for entering basic user details. The fields are described in the table below. The second half is for adding a user group to the user.

Figure 2 - Adding a New User Record.

Basic User Details

The following information can be provided for a user. Please, note that the email address, full name, and system language are the only compulsory details.

Is Active

Denotes whether an account is active or not. Must be enabled.

System Language

Preferred system language to use. Currently, only English is available.

Email Address

The email address assigned by SOCOTEC UK.

Organisation Unit

The organisation unit the user belongs to.

Contact Info

Creates an Account record against the user. (optional)

Full Name

Name of the user.

Job Title

Job title of the user.

Billable Rate

Hourly rate of the user (optional).

Signature

The user’s electric signature.

After entering the compulsory details and saving the record, the User Details grid at the bottom becomes available.

Adding User Groups

Since CymBuild is a software that is shared by many disciplines across SOCOTEC, user groups are a way to manage various things: what kind of content a user can access and what privileges they have. For example:

Prevents users from one discipline being able to see records that belong to another discipline.

Restricts normal users to access sections that meant for super users/administrators.

Limi'
+ N'ts the type of operations they can carry out in the system.

To add a user group, simply click “New” and select the desired user group. This will be then automatically assigned to user.

Figure 3 - Assigning a User Group to a User.

