Contents

Overview3

When can I use batch edit?3

How to use it?3

Overview

Batch edit is a functionality supported by grids in CymBuild that allows changing a common attribute for several records simultaneously. This enables the user to save time on manual processing, since they do not have change information on a one-on-one basis. Imagine we have ten records that all need the assignee property changed. Instead of opening each record and then changing the field, we can just select the records in question and with a single operation the attribute will be updated for all of them.

When can I use batch edit?

A grid that supports batch edit will have a blue button, labelled as “Bulk Update” in the top right corner, next to the “New” button.

Note

A grid might support bulk edit, but if it has no record, the button will not appear as there is nothing to edit!

How to use it?

To illustrate how to use the functionality, we will be using the “Activity” record type.

Once we click the bulk update button, a modal will open with the original grid in it as a dynamic batch grid , which allows the selection of one or more records through the included checkbox on each line.

Once the records that need updating have been identified, select the corresponding line items by ticking the checkboxes next to them, then click “Next” to proceed. If you wish to exit without making changes, click “Cancel” to close the modal.

On the next screen, a new modal will appear displaying all the attributes that can be modified. Initially, these attributes are disabled. To enable an attribute for editing, check the box on the left-hand side of the corresponding field. This can be done for as many fields as deemed necessary. Once a field is enabled, simply select/enter the desired value and click “Confirm”. The user will then be prompted to confirm their selection.

Note

In certain cases, a user may enable a field for editing but find that no options are available in the combo box (dropdown field). This issue can arise due to discrepancies in how the records are configured. While one record may support a specific value, others might not, res'
+ N'ulting in the absence of selectable options.

After confirming the selection, a loading screen will appear. Once the process is complete, the modal will close. If the update is successful, the changes will be reflected in the grid. However, if the operation fails, it may be due to permission issues.

How to Enable Batch Edit for a Grid?

Note

To enable the functionality for a given grid, it must be done through the Development section which is only accessible with the appropriate permissions – specifically, super user permission

Note
A grid might support bulk edit, but if it has no record, the button will not appear  as there is nothing to edit !
Note
