Overview

Job types can be created to fit the specific process requirements for an organisational unit – milestones the project should include activities that need to be carried, or even defining the individuals with certain roles that will be required for the job.

This document will explain in detail how to set up job types.

Creating a New Job

Entering Initial Information

The section for creation of a new job can be found in the settings area – in the grid drawer, look for the item called “Job Types”. When clicked, a list of already existing jobs should appear. To create a new entry, click the “New” button located in the top right corner.

Figure 1- Main grid for displaying all available job types.

Before we can fully configure the job, some of the basic details need to be entered. If not yet sure about all the details, entering a name should be sufficient that the record can be saved to the system. Below is a table that contains the available fields and their explanation:

Is Active

Denotes if a job type is active, meaning it becomes a selectable choice when adding a service on an enquiry. Ensure this is enabled if you wish to use a job type – otherwise, it will not appear as a selectable option.

Name

Name of the job.

Organisational Unit

The organisation unit the job belongs to – if left empty, the job will

Sequence

Order/position of the job type in the main Job Types grid under settings.

Use Plan Checks

TODO

Use Time Sheets

If enabled, transactions will be charged based on the hours entered and/or the assignee’s billable rate

Assigning Additional Information

Once a job has been saved, three grids should become available to edit at the bottom. These are detailed down below.

Milestone Types

Figure 2 - Modal for adding milestones to job type.

In here, we can add milestones that will be a'
+ N'ssociated with the job type. This means that whenever a new job of a given type is created the system will automatically include this in the “Milestones” section.

Job Type Milestone Types Fields

Milestone Type ID

Dropdown to select from existing milestones in the system. If not present or there is a need to create new ones, the arrow button on the right side can be used to create them.

Sort Order

Defines the order of the milestone on the job. For example, if we have 10 milestones & we assign ‘2’ to a milestone, it will be in the second position from the top.

Description

Description of the milestone – please, note this will not be visible on the job, only when inspecting a line-item in this grid.

An example of a configured milestone template can be found below. It illustrates what the user will see when they navigate to the milestone section on a job.

Figure 3 - Example of what configured milestones will look like on a job.

Job Type Project Roles

Figure 4 - Modal for adding directory roles to a job type.

In here, we can assign different roles that might be of use during the different stages of the job. This can include architects, designers, structural engineers, etc. These will also be visible in a project, given the job itself is linked to one. Like the milestones above, setting the “Sort Order” will define the position of the role.

[TO ADD EXAMPLE]

Activity Types

Akin to milestones, since we can define what kind of activities will be available to choose from for a job type.  Example of what this would like is included below:

Figure 5 - Example of what configured activities would look like on a job.

Using a New Job Type

After a job type has been added, we should be able to use it straightaway when adding an enquiry service. An example – simply called “Test” – has been set up to showcase.

