Overview

This document is intended to illustrate how users can create milestones in CymBuild.

Prerequisites

The user must have the appropriate permission level to be able to access the settings area of the system.

Creating a New Milestone

Like with most things in CymBuild, milestones can be created in the Settings section. Expand the drawer of the settings grid and look for the “Milestone Types” item. Once opened, the user should see a list of already existing milestones – click the “New” button located in the top-right corner of the grid to create a new one. This should open a modal where the details can be entered.

Figure 1 - Modal for creating a new milestone

Altogether, there are three text-based input fields on the left, while on the right-hand side we have a list of checkboxes that control the attributes of the created milestone. Let us break these inputs down in the form of a table.

Text Inputs

Field Name

Description

Required?

Code

Unique code for the milestone

Yes

Name

Name of the milestone that will be displayed in the system.

Yes

Help Text

Used to provide description about the milestone.

No

Checkbox Inputs

Name

Description

Is Active

Used to enable the milestone. If left unchecked, the milestone will not show.

Is Invoice Trigger

If enabled, the milestone can have an invoice request against it.

Has Description

If enabled, the “Description” field becomes available for the milestone to edit.

Has Reference

If enabled, the “Reference” field becomes available for the milestone.

Is Compulsory

TODO

Is Review Required

If enabled, the milestone will have fields pertaining to reviewing.

Has Quoted Hours

If enabled, the milestone can have quoted hours against it.

Include Start

If enabled, the “Start Date/Time” field will be included for the milestone. Used to define when the milestone has started.

Has External Submission

If enabled, the external submission field will be inc'
+ N'luded for the field.

Include Schedule

If enabled, it will include fields related to scheduling

Include Due Date

If enabled, the “Due Date” field will show.

Once the required fields have been completed, save the record, after which the milestone will become available to use.

