How to use it?7

Overview

Since CymBuild stores a large collection of records – specifically, client & asset related – it is important to ensure that there are no duplicate records. For this, a merge functionality has been added which enables the merging of similar/duplicate records into one record.

Locations

Assets Merge Location

The assets merge can be found by going to the “Assets” option in the side menu & selecting “Assets Merge Batch”. Upon opening the drawer, we can see a lists of previously merged asset records.

Figure 1 - Asset merging functionality

Below the merge batch option in the grid drawer, we can also see another one titled “Assets, Possible Duplicates” which – in terms of underlying functionality - is very similar to the manual merging. Except, the system automatically picks up records that are possibly duplicates.

CRM Merge Location

The CRM merge can be found by going to the “CRM” option in the side menu & selecting “Account Merge Batch”.

Figure 2 - Account Merge

What is displayed Is identical to the asset merge – a list of previously created merge requests for CRM records. Unlike assets, we do not have a separate grid for likely duplicates.

Process of Merging Duplicate Records

As the process of merging duplicate records is identical, the below guide can be applied for both use cases. In this case, we will be using the asset merge functionality as example to demonstrate the process, especially since the assets come with the extra grid (possible duplicates) which can be discussed at the end.

Creating a New Merge Request

In the appropriate grid view, we need to click the “New” button located in the top-right corner the screen. This will redirect us to a merge batch screen.

Figure 3 - New button for cr'
+ N'eating a merge

Figure 4 - Merge Batch Screen

As we can see from the screenshot, there are only two compulsory (and editable) fields that need to be specified, which is the two accounts we would like to merge. Once both have been selected, simply click the save button.

Figure 5 - Created merge request.

Approving a Merge

To provide an additional layer of oversight (ensuring that the merge is correct), once the request has been created, it will need to be approved by another user. Only after that the records will merge into one. For this, simply open the existing request & tick the “Is Complete” option & then save the record. The merge will automatically complete afterwards.

Figure 6 - Is Complete field

Possible Duplicates

As mentioned earlier, the assets come with an additional grid view which lists records that are possibly duplicates – this done dynamically by the system by comparing the addresses set between records. If the addresses are similar, the system automatically flags them & then are displayed in the grid seen in the screenshot below.

Figure 7 - Possible duplicates grid

How to use it?

Using this functionality is straightforward: when double-clicking a line item in the grid, a modal is opened with two options in the form of checkboxes: “Is Different” and “Is Duplicate”.

Figure 8 - Possible merge modal

If “Is Different” is selected, the system will just simply exclude the suggestion from the grid. Otherwise, if “Is Duplicate” is selected, the system will merge the records into one & any other record type that uses either asset record out of the two will be updated to reflect the merge.'', IsAuthoritative = 1, IsPublished = 1, PublishedUtc = ''2026-06-03 15:10:48.6268707'', CreatedByUserId = 722, UpdatedByUserId = 722, CreatedUtc = ''2026-06-03 15:10:48.6268707'', UpdatedUtc = ''2026-06-03 15:51:58.7817898'' WHERE ID = 6 AND RowStatus = 1 AND Title = N''TM - Merge Functionality'' AND Slug = N''sharepoint-drives-b-rn0a3cmntewrc6jxnw4s987d1vqr2-reudnhtp5j5cbtgd2quthut4s9ge1vckbz-root-general-training-material-business-process-documentations-tm-crm-account-merge-batch-tm-merge-functionality-1'' AND KnowledgeCategoryId IS NULL
