Overview

In this document, we will be focusing on the accounts section of the Customer Relationship Management section, specifically, how to create new accounts in the system. The document will also include sections where accounts can also be added from.

Adding a New Customer

First, locate the “CRM” in the menu on the left-hand side. A grid will appear with four distinctive options: for this, we will need “Accounts”.

Figure 1- Accounts section in CRM

Creating The Account

To create a new one, click the “New” button located in the top-right corner of the grid. Once clicked, the system will navigate to a new page where we can add the details.

Figure 2 - Account creation page.

As we can see, the only compulsory field that needs to be filled is the name, which should allow us to create a record. Below is a table of fields that are available for us – to keep it simple, the inputs have been divided into three groups as per the three sections in the screenshot.

Account

Account Code (Sage)

Used for exporting transactions in CymBuild. The code is used to map the correct account in Sage.

Name

Name of the account.

Account Status

Can be of four values: Active, Closed, Credit Hold, Prospect.

Parent Account

We can assign an existing account given the one being created belongs to one.

Relationship Manager

Main person in charge of firming relationship with the client/account.

Company Registration Number

Official registration number that is associated with the company the account belongs to.

Main Address

The primary address of the company.

Main Contact

The main contact of the company/account.

Account Type

Is Fire Authority

Committee of local councillors which oversees the policy and service delivery of a fire and rescue services.

Is Local Authority

If the account is local authority (e.g'
+ N'. council)

Is Water Authority

Water supplier

Is Purchase Ledger

Sales ledger tracks money customers owe to the business, while a purchase ledger tracks money the business owes to suppliers.

Is Sales Ledger

Main Details

Main Address

Fields for displaying data only – values are sourced from the grids found at the bottom.

Main Phone

Main E-Mail

Available Grids

Once an account has been saved, three different grids will become available to edit. These are essentially additional information that can be linked to the account itself, such as additional addresses & contacts.

Account Addresses

This grid can be used to add associated addresses to the account. Once an address has been added, the “Main Address” field becomes populated.

Clicking “New” in the grid will bring up the modal above which allows us to add an address, which can be done by clicking the arrow button to the right of the dropdown. The dropdown also allows us to access all previously added addresses that may or may not have relation with the account. If the address that needs adding is already present, simply select it in the dropdown and then click Save/Save and Exit.

