Purpose

This document is intended to give a detailed explanation around the process of creating a job from the initial enquiry phase.

Overview

The first step begins after the enquiry from a client has been received by the team. An enquiry is created with information pertaining to basic client information.

The enquiry has been accepted, now the quote must be prepared which can be completed from withing the enquiry.

Once a quote is completed & sent to the client

If approved, the job can be created from either the quote or the enquiry itself.

If rejected, mark the quote as such

In both cases, we mark the quote as accepted/rejected through the enquiry instead of the quote

Creating an Enquiry

Creating an enquiry can be done from the main enquiry grid by clicking the “New” button located in the top-right corner of the screen. Upon clicking it, the user is redirected to a new page with the enquiry template loaded.

Figure 1 - "New" button for creating an enquiry.

Prior to saving the record for the first time, the only required field that needs to be completed is the “Current Project Stage”. After performing a save, the SharePoint site will be created and the “Enquiry Services” grid will become available to edit where we can add the job type based on the what the client has requested – these can be viewed by double clicking the line item in the grid.

EnquiryEnquiry

Enquiry

Enquiry

Figure 2 – Enquiry Page: Enquiry Services

The following three pieces of information that can be defined for an enquiry service can be found in the table below:

Job Type

The type of job required (e.g.  CDM PD, H&S, etc)

Start RIBA Stage

The starting RIBA stage for a job

End RIBA Stage

The last RIBA stage that concludes a job.

For an added service, we can see values in the grid which will be relevant to the quote later down the line. These are the quote number, the net '
+ N'amount of it, and finally the status (columns “Quote”, “Quote Net”, and “Status”). Furthermore, once a quote is created, opening a line item will bring up the same modal as shown in figure 2, but with additional information relating to the quote.

Note

Throughout the different stages, we will have to refer to this section. For example, in the quote stage, the date on which the quote was accepted by a client will have to be set here before a job can be created – this is by design as enquiries are meant to hold key information that traverses the different stages.

Figure 3 - Enquiry Services keeping track of quote related information

Once the required service(s) and necessary information have been added, the enquiry can be converted to a quote. For this, the enquiry must first be marked for a quote review which can be done by ticking the “Is Ready For Quote Review” checkbox. If there is missing information that is required, the corresponding fields will be highlighted in red after clicking said checkbox.

A blue data pill will also appear just under enquiry number at the top, signifying that the enquiry is ready to be turned into a quote.

Figure 4 - Data pill

To convert the enquiry, locate the Tasks menu button in the top-right corner and select the “Create Quote(s) From Enquiry” option from the drop-down menu.

Figure 5 - (Tasks menu) Option for converting an enquiry to a quote.

Upon successful creation, a green status message will appear at the top which informs the user that the quote has been created.

Figure 6 - Status message for a successfully created quote.

The created quote can be accessed by navigating down to service(s) added on the enquiry itself in the Enquiry Services grid and double clicking the added service. A modal will open as described in figure 2 with additional information pertaining to the newly created quote.

EnquiryEnquiry

Enquiry

Enquiry

Figure 7 – Enquiry page: Enquiry Services with additional information

To access the quote, click the arrow button next to the “Quote” field.

Figure 8 - Click the arrow button to access the quote.

Turning a Quote into a Job

For a quote, most information will be sourced from the enquiry stage, only a limited amount of information will need adding - . First and foremost, a quote item must be added.

QuoteQuote

Quote

Quote

