Overview

The following document is intended to explain the installation process for CymBuild on mobile devices – this will include installing both the Test and Live version of the software.

Prerequisites

First and foremost, to access either the Test or the Live system, we will need to have Chrome installed - by default, mobile devices provided by SOCOTEC are restricted to only have the Google app, something which is mainly used to perform quick searches on Google where needed. This is important since it means that we cannot access websites directly by typing the address in the search bar.

To install Chrome, the first step is to open the Google app – below, you can see the icon for it in figure 1.

Figure 1 - Google App Icon

Figure 2 - Opening Google App

Once opened, you should see something similar as above in figure 2 – look for the search bar located at the top & search for “Chrome”. Scroll down until you see a section titled “Apps” with “Google Chrome” in it (figure 3, highlighted in red)

Figure 3 - Apps section where Chrome can be downloaded

Upon tapping “Google Chrome”, a window should come up with the option to install the browser as seen in Figure 4. After this step, you should have Chrome ready to use.

Note

Please note that the screenshots seen in this document were captured on a personal mobile device which has Chrome enabled by default – the screenshot only shows the “Open” option in figure 4, but you will have install option there.

Figure 4 - Window to install Chrome from

Installing CymBuild from Chrome

Considerations

This section will go in detail on installing both the Test and Live version of CymBuild. The steps for both are identical, but there is a key consideration to '
+ N'keep in mind: While the Live version is accessible without being connected to either a SOCOTEC Wi-Fi network or the SOCOTEC VPN, this is not the case for the Test site version.

As such, if you wish to install the Test site version, please ensure that you are connected to the SOCOTEC Wi-Fi network on your mobile device!

Installation Steps

Now that Chrome is installed, the first step is to access the either the Test or the Live site. Below is a table with their respective web address:

Test

https://bre.socotec.co.uk:9502

Live

https://bre.socotec.co.uk:9602/

Once the page has loaded, the next step is to access the options in Chrome. For this, locate the three vertical dots in the upper right corner of the browser as marked in figure 5. After tapping it, you should see several options as seen in figure 6.

Figure 5 - Accessing the options menu in Chrome

Figure 6 - Available options in Chrome

Before CymBuild is installed, please ensure that the “Desktop site” is not enabled – if it is, CymBuild will not apply the mobile formatting. Once that is in order, simply tap the “Add to home screen” option, after which CymBuild will be ready to use.

Distinguishing between the Test & Live Mobile App

If you happen to have both the Test and Live app installed, you will find that both the icons will be the same, which might make distinguishing the two not as straightforward. The best way to do this is paying attention to the very top of the screen – the test site will have an orange bar running through the screen (figure 7) while the Live site will have no coloured bar at all.

Figure 7 - Test site with an orange bar at the top

Figure 8 - Live system without a coloured bar

