Once the document has been placed in the folder, it is ready to be referenced in CymBuild. To create a reference, we will need to access the dedicated settings area which can be located by going to Settings > Merge Documents. From here, click the “New” button located in the top right corner – this will bring up a new modal.

Starting with the tabs, there are two available. The first tab (Merge Documents) consists of fields that we need to configure to create the reference in the system as well as nested items (images & pictures), while the second tab – called Merge Fields – will contain a list of predefined merge fields that the user can reference in the document itself. When first creating a reference, this list will not be available. For that, we need to first configure the reference.

