Generating a Merge Document

To generate the document, simply navigate to the record type you assigned it to. In this example, we will be using an enquiry to get a document called “Fee Proposal”. On the enquiry page, look for the Task button. Hover over the button and select “Document Tasks” from the dropdown menu.

Figure 15 - Accessing merge document generator section.

After clicking it, a modal should appear with two different input fields – the top one is for filtering the search result while the bottom one lists all documents available for the record type of enquiry.

Figure 16 - Searching for a merge document.

Since we know the document required is simply called “Fee Proposal”, we can use the top field to limit the search result in the bottom one. Once the document is selected, press “Generate Document”.

Figure 17 - Selecting a merge document.

On the next screen of the modal, we are prompted to select between the format of the generated document, which can either be Docx or PDF. Clicking either will automatically start the process.

Figure 18 - Selecting the output format for merge document.

