How to use it?3

Overview

To improve user experience and efficiency when entering address related information, a tool – which we refer to as postcode lookup – has been integrated into CymBuild. It allows users to search for addresses by either the postcode or parts of the address (e.g. just the street name) which then returns a list of suggested addresses from which upon selecting one, all the details – along with handy details like the UPRN & authorities – are filled in, meaning it eliminates the need for manual entry.

Locations

The functionality is only available in a few places which might change depending on the requirements from the business units. Currently, it can be found on the asset and enquiry page. Generally, when the lookup tool is available, you should see a button in the header of a given section which will be labelled as “Address Lookup”.

Assets

On the asset page, the button can be found in the “Address detail” section.

Figure 1 - The Address lookup button

For enquiries, the button does not show automatically & must be enabled by ticking the “Enter New … Details” after which the button becomes visible. We have the checkbox for the following sections:

Asset Details

Client & Agents Details

Finance Account Details

Figure 2 - Enquiries: enabling the "Address Lookup" button for a given section.

How to use it?

Using the tool is quite simple. Once the “Address Lookup” button has been clicked, a window should appear as seen below. Firstly, at the top of the window, a blue bar has been included – when clicked, it should include helpful information on how to use it.

Figure 3 - Popup window for postcode lookup

Further down, we have a text field where we enter the postcode/street name and a dropdown to its right for selecting the country of origin. On the right-hand side, we find a list of read-only fields which will populate once an address has been selected. This is simply for previewing the details to make sure it is the correct one.

Once we have entered the required information, we just need to click t'
+ N'he search button underneath. An additional dropdown will appear from which we can select an address– click “Confirm”, after which the read-only fields should populate.

Figure 4 - Read-only fields populating

Once the read-only fields are populated, we have two options: if the details look correct, we can click “Done” after which the window will close and the fields on the main record (e.g. the asset) will populate, or if needed, we can amend the details. For this, click the “Amend address” button, after which the read-only fields become editable. When done editing, click “Done”.

