Overview

The Filtered Quoting grid enhances the standard quoting grid by adding status indicators, quick filters, and ordering options. These features help users quickly identify relevant quotes, track required actions, and organise data more efficiently.

Location

To access the grid, click “Quoting” in the side menu and select “Filtered Quoting”

Figure 1 - Location of the Filtered Quoting area

Functionality

Below is a detailed description of the features the new grid comes with.

Status Labels

Status indicators have been added to the grid with the purpose of flagging any record that requires chasing, which happens when the appropriate workflow (e.g. 1st Chase) has been added to the record. In this case, the line in the grid will have a filled red circle under the “Status” column.  If there is no chase required, the status indicator will be green. A helper section has been also added to the grid to provide explanation as can be seen from the screenshot below.

Figure 2 - Status Indicators

Quick Filters

Figure 3 - Available quick filters.

Three buttons have been added to allow a quick and easy way to filter data down – specifically, what period the data should be from. For example, the “Last 7 days” will return records created in the last 7 days, while it is the last 90 days from the other button.

Alternatively, we have the “Custom Range” button which will include data between two (inclusive) dates.

Figure 4 - Custom range filtering.

Ordering

Figure 5 - Ordering dropdown.

Lastly, we have the ordering dropdown located on the far right of the grid. This allows the data to be ordered in a specific way. Currently, there are four options available:

