Overview

The Quote duplication functionality has now been proceeded by revision, as you would now need to Duplicate the Enquiry itself instead. This document is intended to explain how this works from a user’s perspective.

Process

Instead of duplicating a quote, a new functionality has been added whereby the quote is revised instead. Like duplication, a new quote is created with all the relevant information copied over – some of the key differences being are the quote number and how they are displayed and or accessed.

Creating a Quote Revision

Like duplication, a quote can be revised through the Task button which can be found in the top-right corner of the quote record. Hovering over the button will show a dropdown with various options – locate the “Revise Quote” option.

Figure 1 - "Quote Revision" option for the Task menu button.

After clicking it, a message will appear at the top notifying the user that the quote is being revised, followed by a success message, after which the page is redirected to the new quote.

Figure 2 - Success message for Creating Revision

Distinguishing a Quote Revision

A revised quote will have the revision number located next to the quote number in parentheses on the Quoting grid. For example, if the number is (5), that means five revisions have been created so far. This is important, since when performing a revision, the original quote number is kept & the appended revision number is used to distinguish between original and revised quotes (or even between multiple revisions)

Figure 3 - A revised quote as seen on the "All Quotes" grid.

The same applies to when viewing the “Enquiry Services” grid on an enquiry – a revision number is also shown when opening an enquiry service, Note only the latest revision is shown.

Figure 4 - Enquiry Service item with a revised quote

Figure 5 - Enquiry Service: the quote is revised as seen from the number in parentheses next to the quote number.

Accessing the Revise'
+ N'd Quote

With the new process, some of the key information for quotes can only be set through the enquiry, specifically the enquiry services grid found at the bottom of the enquiry record. This is where we can set the acceptance/rejection date for example, or even access the created quote that is associated with the original enquiry service (e.g. Figure 4) .

When we revise a quote, the data pertaining to the original enquiry service will be updated – no additional line-item will be added to it. Instead, the most up to date revision will be shown.

Accessing the previous Quote revisions

With the new process, these previous Quote revisions are not closed but instead left for you the user to decide what there status requirements are. You can view the additional Quote Revisions from the Quoting Navigation Grids:'', IsAuthoritative = 1, IsPublished = 1, PublishedUtc = ''2026-06-03 15:10:55.4715967'', CreatedByUserId = 722, UpdatedByUserId = 722, CreatedUtc = ''2026-06-03 15:10:55.4715967'', UpdatedUtc = ''2026-06-03 15:52:04.3924281'' WHERE ID = 22 AND RowStatus = 1 AND Title = N''TM Template'' AND Slug = N''sharepoint-drives-b-rn0a3cmntewrc6jxnw4s987d1vqr2-reudnhtp5j5cbtgd2quthut4s9ge1vckbz-root-general-training-material-business-process-documentations-tm-quote-revision-tm-template-1'' AND KnowledgeCategoryId IS NULL
