Overview

The following document aims to explain how to perform a Sage export in the Finance section of CymBuild, which will produce a CSV file that can be submitted to Sage by the finance team.

Prerequisites

To be able to access this section on CymBuild, the user will need to have the “Finance” user group assigned to them – the lack of this will result in the grid being hidden from the user.

Generating a Sage Export

First, locate the “Finance” section in the side menu – this will bring up the main finance page with the corresponding grid which should have five drawers in total. If needed, expand the drawers & locate the one called “Sage Export”. Once clicked, a list of previously generated exports should be shown.

To create a new export, click the “New” button located in the top-right corner of the grid - a modal should appear.

Field

Description

Required?

Inclusive To Date

Generates an export to the date selected (inclusively)

Yes

Organisation Unit Id

The organisational unit to create an export for

Yes

Export Data

Read-only field – displays the export.

No

After completing the required fields, click “Save” to generate the export. Once completed, a green success message will appear and the “Export Data” field should populate with the output (this can be used to have a preview without having to download the file) – to download the csv, select the “Generate CSV Download” option from the Tasks menu button.

Figure 1 - Generate CSV Download

Viewing Previously Generated Exports

Previously generated exports can be viewed through the sage export grid – for this, double-click a line-item which should bring up the same model when creating a new one – once open, the CSV can be downloaded the same way as when creating a new export, through the “Generate CSV Download” button.

