Overview

The scheduler is a type of calendar that users can utilize to keep track of not only their own upcoming activities or holidays, but also those of other members on their team. This document is intended to explain how to use the scheduler from a user''''s perspective.

Accessibility

The scheduler can be accessed by locating “Schedule” in the side menu and then selecting the “Team Availability” tab at the top.

Figure 1 - Accessing the scheduler

Layout

Figure 2 - Scheduler page

Altogether, we have four different sections on the page – these will be explained in order from top to bottom.

Legend

Figure 3 - The legend

The legend is a small, non-interactive section that explains the meaning of the different coloured slots in the scheduler. For example, an orange slot indicates a user is absent during AM hours, while a red slot signifies a PM absence. Upcoming activities are shown in blue. Bank holidays are marked with red slots across the day, and weekends are displayed in grey.

Filters

Figure 4 - Available filters

Currently, there are three checkboxes and a multiselect field that can be utilized:

Checkboxes:

Show Work: If disabled, scheduled activities will not be shown on the calendar.

Show Absences: If disabled, scheduled absences (added by the users) will not be shown on the calendar.

Show Public Holidays: If disabled, public holidays will not be shown on the calendar.

Multiselect:

Filter By Person: This dropdown allows you to filter the calendar by person. It contains a list of all users currently displayed in the calendar. By selecting one or more users, the calendar view will update to show appointments for only those selected. To reset the view and show all users again, simply deselect all selected users.

Calendar View

Figure 5 - Calendar view

The main calendar view where data is displayed – as explaine'
+ N'd in the Legend section, each appointment – depending on its type and the time it takes place – might have a different colour code.

Navigation Buttons

In the top right corner of the calendar, there are three grouped buttons: a “Today” button, which takes the user to the current date, and backward and forward buttons, which allow the user to navigate through time.

Figure 6 - Time navigation buttons

View Mode Buttons

There are currently four different views we can utilize: day, week, month, and timeline. In terms of functionality, there is no distinction between either of them.

Figure 7 - View modes

My Absences

Figure 8 - My absences grid

The absences grid can be used to keep track of all manually added absences – this does not include upcoming activities, and a user can only see their own absences.

Operations

Adding Absences

Figure 9 - Absence details modal

To add an absence, simply double-click on the desired cell in the schedule. Each row represents a person, and each column corresponds to a specific date and time slot (AM or PM). Double-clicking opens a modal where you can enter the absence details. At the top of the modal, the person''''s name will appear in blue, followed by a dropdown to select the type of absence (e.g., meeting, holiday). The start and end times are automatically set based on the selected slot - 8:30 AM to 1:00 PM for AM, and 1:00 PM to 5:00 PM for PM - but these times can be adjusted if needed (e.g. booking out the whole day)

Viewing Absences

To view an absence, simply double click it which will open the modal described above with the details populated. Currently, only user added absences can be viewed in the modal.

Figure 10 - Viewing an existing appointment

For upcoming activities, we can hover over the appointment which will give us key details such as the job number it pertains to and the start time.

Figure 11 - Key information for upcoming details

Users can also view their absences through the “My Absences” grid at the bottom of the page by double-clicking an entry in the grid.

Editing Absences

Once an existing absence has been opened, simply change the desired field(s) where needed and click “Confirm” – the absence will be then updated.

Removing Absences

To remove an absence, the “My Absences” grid can be utilized. Please note, that a user can only remove their own absences but not others. Simply double click the appointment in the grid & select the “Delete” option under the Tasks button.

Figure 12 - Deleting an absence

Adding Absence Types

By default, there are three different types of absence types: holiday, maternity leave, and meeting. If a new type is required, it can be added through the settings section in CymBuild. Please note that you will need appropriate permissions to access this the sections.

When in the settings, simply look for the drawer type called “Non-Activity Types” and click “New” in the top right corner of the grid – this will bring up a modal where you can enter the absence type.

Figure 13 - Settings: non-activity type grid

