Introduction

This document has been created to help developers understand how CymBuild works as well to have something to refer to when in doubt about the functionality of the code.

Overview

CymBuild is made of 6 solutions, each with a particular purpose in mind. For example, we have the API solution, which is mainly used to describe proto definitions, EF for interacting with the database, PWA for the front-end, and so on. In this documentation, we will be covering each of these solutions in depth.

Helpful documentations

PWA

Overview

The PWA solution is entirely devoted to the front-end, meaning that all UI components are stored here (apart from those stored in the components shared solution). This includes the buttons, input fields, lists, tables, etc.

Solution Structure

Properties

Contains the publisher profile configuration. More profiles can be added if necessary. This is only used when the solution is being exported for production.

Wwwroot

Classes

Contains custom class definitions that might be used in the solution. For example, the modal implementation or the app configuration.

