Overview

This guide provides a guide for the new features and workflows introduced in Cymbuild Version 26.1.

1. Bid Team Review Notifications

Purpose

Automated email notifications are sent to the Bid Team when enquiries require review.

Creating an Enquiry Requiring Bid Team Review:

Navigate to Enquiries and create a new Enquiry

Complete the following mandatory fields:

Lead organization (e.g., Fire Engineering)

Signatory

Project stage

Client Information

Asset

Description of work

Value

Job type

Add the Enquiry Service

Change the inquiry status to "Bid Team Review"

Click Save and Exit

What Happens Next:

The Enquiry has data pills at the top of the screen

Bid Team Review and User Action Required

An automated notification email is sent to designated Bid Team members

The email includes:

Organizational unit

Workflow status

Actor (person who created the inquiry)

Client name

Project details

Loca'
+ N'tion

Asset information

Any comments entered

Due date (if applicable)

"View Record" button linking directly to the inquiry

Sample Email:

Authorization Process

For Bid Team Reviewers:

Navigate to the inquiry requiring review

Go to the Authorization area

Select one of three options:

Review - Opens a window with details of the Enquiry to Approve or Reject

Approve - No comments required; automatically changes status to "Bid Team Review Approved" and "Ready for Quote"

Reject - Comments are mandatory; sends rejection notification to Operations team

The system will change the status to Ready for Quote

You can now convert the Enquiry to a Quote

2. Quote Authorisation:

The same review process applies for quoting, a Quote with “For Review” status will be sent to authorisers

Navigate to the Quote (after client acceptance)

Add the product/service details

Change Quote status to For Review and select Save and Exit

The User Action Required Data pill will pop up at the top of the screen

A notification will be sent to the authorisers with details of the quote similar to the enquiry

Template Example:

Authorization Process

Go to the Authorization area

Select one of three options:

Review - Opens a window with details of the Quote to Approve or Reject

Approve - No comments required; automatically changes status to "Bid Team Review Accepted"

Reject - Comments are mandatory; sends rejection notification to Operations team

This changes the Quote Record to Review Team Accepted

Finalise the Fee proposal Form and send to client.

Change Quote status to sent

3. Invoice Scheduling and Automation

Purpose

Set up automated invoicing structures when a quote is won.

Steps

Setting Up Invoice Schedule (After Quote Acceptance):

Once the job has been Accepted by the Client

Navigate to the Quote

Go to the Invoicing area

Select Invoice Schedule tab, select New

Input a description

Choose the invoicing structure:

Manual - Invoices raised manually

Activity/Milestone Based - Automated upon activity completion/ Milestone Completion/ Activity and Milestone Completion

Monthly-Drawdown - Based on agreed payment schedule

Percentage Based - Based on percentage of completion

RIBA Stage Based - Based on project stage completion

Note: If no invoicing schedule is created and assigned to a product, the system will default to Manual Invoicing schedule which can be changed at the Job stage

For Activity/Milestone Based Invoicing:

Select "Activity/Milestone Based"

Choose trigger: "On Activity Completion" or "On Milestone Completion" or “On Activity and Milestone Completion”

E.g. In this case select On Activity Completion

System will automatically raise invoice requests when activities are marked complete

Invoice requests still require Finance approval

For Monthly Invoicing:

Select "Monthly Drawdowns" and Save

This opens up the Invoice scheduling Monthly Area, select New

Enter First Invoice Date

Enter End Date for invoicing period

Enter the Total Value agreed with the Client and save

System will spread the value across the months for automatic generation of monthly invoice requests

Assigning Invoice Schedules to Products

Navigate to the Quote Items in the Quote Details Tab

Select the product to assign an invoicing schedule

Monthly draw down assignment

Select Monthly Draw down and save and exit

Activity Completion Assignment (Another product was added to show for this use case)

Select Activity/Milestone Based, and save and exit

Change the status to customer accepted

Converting to Job:

Navigate to Tasks

Click Convert to Job

The jobs will be created with their invoicing structure

4. New Fields: Sectors and Markets

Purpose

Categorize quotes and jobs by industry sector and geographical market .

Sectors:

Industry classification for the project

Markets'
+ N':

Geographical location: UK or International

How to Complete

In the Quote or Job record

Locate Sectors field

Select appropriate industry sector

Locate Markets field

Select UK or International

Note: These fields are currently optional and will pull through to the job.

5. Job Financial Overview

Each job has a financial overview at the top of the window that shows users financial info to help keep track of the job finances

Remaining Fees

Outstanding Amount with and Without VAT

Overdue fees by Aging Buckets

6. Automated Activity-Based Invoicing

Purpose

Eliminate duplicate work by automatically generating invoice requests when billable activities are completed.

Steps

Activity Creation:

Navigate to the Job

Change the Job Status to Job Started

Mark the Acceptance / Contract Documentation Received field

Go to Activities tab

Create activities with:

Title: Activity name (e.g., "Site Visit", "Fire Safety Strategy")

Type: Activity type (e.g., Meeting, Site Visit)

Status- Tentative/ Confirmed

Invoicing value (if billable)

Start and End date

Notes: Detailed description of activity

Save and Exit

Activity In Progress:

Navigate to Jobs → Select your job

Go to Activities tab

Double-click the activity

Change status to "In Progress"

Save and Exit

Activity Completion:

Navigate to Jobs → Select your job

Go to Activities tab

Double-click the activity

Change status from "In Progress" to "Complete"

Add detailed notes including:

Date of activity

Contact names

Specific details (e.g., who received the report)

Any agreements with client

Click Save and Exit

What Happens Next:

If the activity is billable, an invoice request is automatically generated and appears in the Fee Tab for the Job

Double click Invoice Request to see more details

The invoice request also appears in the Finance area for approval

No need to manually raise an invoice from the Fees tab

Technical team can continue working without additional administrative tasks

