Settings

The settings menu is used not necessarily to change the settings for the signed in user but rather to keep & manage systemwide settings in one place – as such, not everyone has permission to access it.

NOTE:

Whether a user can access the “Settings” menu or not is linked to permission levels – this might mean that you will not be able to access it.

A few examples of settings that can be changed:

User settings (name, emails, units they belong to)

Organisation unit’s setup

Documents

Quote related information.

