Introduction

Concursus Yielding Metadata for BUILDing & Real Estate

Purpose

This document aims to outline the core features of CymBuild from the user''''s perspective, ensuring smooth software use and serving as a helpful reference when needed. It starts with an overview of the platform, helping users navigate CymBuild''''s layout with ease. Then, the document introduces essential components like tables, buttons, and filters. This introduction is crucial for two reasons: firstly, these elements are the building blocks of the application, present throughout various sections. Secondly, understanding them ensures that users can utilize them effectively.

Once the basics are understood, users should feel confident navigating the system. The next steps are to:

Explain how to carry out various processes, such as creating an inquiry or quote.

Provide a troubleshooting guide.

Offer answers to frequently asked questions.

Finally, a comprehensive list of available resources will be included.

OverviewWhen launching the application, the user is greeted by the Home/Dashboard page. The navigation menu is located on the left side, while the quick access sections are displayed on the right.

Navigation Bar

Figure 1 – Navigation Bar

Home:

Directs the user to the widget dashboard.

My Work:

Displays all jobs associated with the user.

Projects:
'
+ N'
Projects link multiple related Enquires, Quotes and Jobs of a real-world project. These may belong to one of more clients or agents but are part of the same physical construction project.

Schedule:

Opens Team Schedule & Team Availability where the user can add and track upcoming activities in the system. (Note: As of the writing of this document, Outlook Calendar has not yet been synchronised.)

CRM:

Customer Relationship Management: Shows a list of all customers in the system.

Structures:

(Properties/UPRN) Provides a list of sites where work has been conducted by SOCOTEC. It includes site addresses, unique property reference numbers (UPRNs), authorities, and more.

Enquiries:

Displays a list of all received enquiries, regardless of their status. This is the initial stage of job creation and is always required. An enquiry progresses to a quote.

Quoting:

Shows all quotes available in the system. Quotes originate from enquiries and can convert into jobs.

Jobs:

Provides a list of all jobs added

Shows a list of projects with all the relevant information pertaining to them, which are generated from completed quotes.

Authorisation

Grid area where records awaiting approval can be found

Finance:

Lists previous transactions throughout the system, as well as those specific to the user. Users can also export invoices for importing into Sage.

Settings:

Provides access to various system settings.

