Customer Relationship Management (CRM)

Provides a list of customers with their contact details. Altogether, there are four available tabs:

Account:

Main customer related information can be found here, such as name, account status, address, etc. (Figure 49)

Further down, we also have:

Account Addresses: Addresses can be stored against the customer. (Figure 50)

Account Contacts: Storing contact information against a person or a group of people, such as name, position, email, etc. (Figure 51)

Account Memos: Memos can be added for an account.(Figure 52)

Finance:

Finance related information can be stored, such as pre'
+ N'vious transactions, as well as the turnover.(Figure 53)

Finance related memos can also be added here.(Figure 54)

Contracts:

Contracts associated with the account in question.(Figure 55)

History:

Associated enquiries, quotes, and jobs to the account.(Figure 56)

