NOTE: Once a quote has been created from an enquiry, the quote number can be found on the enquiry record it originates from. To do this, open the enquiry and scroll down to the “Enquiry Details” grid found at the bottom of the page. Figure  61 - Finding the quote number on an enquiry record.
Begin by creating a new quote section under “Quote Details”. Fill out all the compulsory fields  à  click Save. Once saved, the “Quote Details” should become available to edit. Add necessary item(s) to the section. Once the quote is ready, tick “Is Final (Ready to Send)”  à  Save. All fields  outside the  q uote  s tatus  p anel  should now become read-only and cannot be edited. Quote  Section : The following  areas are available under  Q uote  S ection: Sections : List of  sections containing  information on the job requirement and any  relevant  product  items.  ( See the information section with   Figure   64  &  65  below ) Fee D rawdown : Shows  the  total  values  for  each RIBA stage  of the quote based on sections  above. Job Creation Summary : Shows  all the Jobs that are to be created once quote has been finalised . This will aid the user in understanding if Sections are consolidated before generating the jobs.  (Figure  66 ) Created Jobs : Links to the job(s) created from the quote. Quote Memos : The user can add a memo to the record. Quote Key Dates : The user can add key dates  with details . | Figure  62 - Quote Page Figure  63 - Quote Details Grid.
INFORMATION                                                                                                                                                                                      Before converting a quote into a job, it is important to mention the functionality to consolidate jobs that are entered into the Quote Details section. In the “Quote Details” section, under the drawer “Section”, the user can add these jobs, but it is important to acknowledge that by  producing   a quote will create the same  number  of job s  as the number of items present in the list  (Figure  64 ) .  Figure  64 - Quote Details Section. To tackle this,  open each task  from the list and  tick the ‘Consolidate Jobs’ . This will create only one job record type which will hold all the jobs  that are marked as Consolidate  (Figure  65 ) .  Figure  65 - Consolidate Jobs. You can confirm the jobs  are  created by viewing the Job Creation Summary (Figure  66 ) Figure  66  - Job creation summary.
