Job : Holds information pertaining to the job itself. This includes the description, job status, both client & agent details, etc. (Figure  69 ) Fees : Holds payment/transaction information, broken down into three categories:  (Figure  70 ) Project D etails : Pe ople  involved in the job (and their contact information) can be found and added here – for example, architects, structural engineers, designers, etc.  Additionally, we also have the “Project Key Dates” table as well. (Figure  71 ) Milestones : Milestones of the project can be managed here – adding new ones as well as excluding existing ones, marking them as completed. Both Activities and Actions can also be added from this tab. These will be reflected on the “Job” tab at the top. (Figure  72 ) Activities : Job related activities that need to be carried & are integral part of the process. This can include sending emails, meetings, inspections, etc. (Figure  73 ) Actions : Unlike activities, actions can be added that are not necessarily part of the job process that require further action. For example, during an inspection, the fire door is discovered not to be shutting properly and must be fixed. (Figure  74 ) | Figure  69 - Job. Figure  70 - Fees. Figure  71 - Project D etails . Figure  72 - Milestones. Figure  73  - Activities. Figure  74  - Actions.
