Installation

In this section, the aim is to give an overview as to how CymBuild can be downloaded from the browser and installed locally on a machine.

Converting CymBuild into an installed application (Optional)

The steps are simple:

Installation using Chrome:

Once CymBuild has been opened in the browser, locate the following icon in the address bar.

Once clicked, Chrome will prompt you whether you would like to install CymBuild. Click “Install”.

Within seconds of clicking the Install button, a new window should open with the dashboard. Additionally, - if using Windows - a popup message should show which prompts the user if they would like CymBuild to be pinned to their taskbar.

To open the app, simply locate it on your work device and launch it.

Installation using Edge:

Once CymBuild has been opened in the browser, locate the following icon in the address bar.

Once clicked, Edge will prompt you whether you would like to install CymBuild. Click “Install”.

Within seconds of clicking the Install button, a new window should open with the dashboard.

A popup message should also be shown with various options. The first two options (pinning to taskbar & start) should already be ticked. A desktop shortcut can also be created in addition with having the application start after the user has logged into their device. These are optional!

When ready, click allow.

To open the app, simply locate it on your device and launch it.

Basic Operations of The Software

This chapter is broken down into two separate sections: Components and Basic Operations.In the first section, – labelled as “components” – the aim is to cover the different components the user encounters while performing different operations (e.g. creating a quote, enquiry, etc.).

This chapter is divided into two sections: Components and Basic Operations.

Components Section:

This section '
+ N'aims to explain the various components that users will encounter while performing different tasks (e.g., creating a quote or enquiry), whether it''''s a dropdown, textbox, etc.

NOTE:

The information provided in the component section serves as the foundation for the next section, afterwards – the basic operations.

In the second half of the chapter, the different operations/processes are covered so that the user may not only become aware of where they need to navigate to initiate said processes, but to also be able to refer of the steps required to complete the processes – these will be explained step-by-step.

Basic Operations Section:

This section describes different processes (e.g., creating enquiries, invoices, jobs, etc.) so that users understand where to navigate to start these processes and have a step-by-step guide for completing them.

Components

In terms of functionality, there are essentially two kinds of components: one providing the user with information pertaining to the project they are working on, while the second kind accepts input from the user.

Throughout the use of CymBuild, the user will have to interact with various input fields to not only input data but to navigate across the various record types.

