Earlier in this document, the tabs found in the job section were briefly touched on, although the exact functionalities were not discussed.

Job:

Holds information pertaining to the job itself. This includes the description, job status, both client & agent details, etc.(Figure 56)

Fees:

Holds payment/transaction information, broken down into three categories:

(Figure 57)

Project Directory:

Persons involved in the job (and their contact information) can be found and added here – for example, architects, structural engineers, designers, etc.(Figure 58)

Milestones:

Milestones of the project can be managed here – adding new ones as well as excluding existing ones, marking them as completed. Both Activities and Actions can also be added from this tab. These will be reflected on the “Job” tab at the top.(Figure 59)

Activities:

Job related activities that need to be carried & are integral part of the process. This can include sending emails, meetings, inspections, etc.(Figure 60)

Actions:

Unlike activities, actions can be added that are not necessarily part of the job process that require further action. For example, during an inspection, the fire door is discovered not to be shutting properly and must be fixed.(Figure 61)

