NOTE:

Transactions can only be created from the “All Transaction” section – “My Invoicing” will not have the option.

Creating New Transaction

Enter all compulsory fields.

Only accounts with a Sage Account code are valid for selection.

Next, save the Transaction.

This will enable both the “Transaction Details” & “Transaction Finance Memo” sections further down the page.

Figure 62 – Creating a transaction.

Creating a Sage Export

From the drawer, select “Sage Export” & select “New”.

Select the date to which you would like to export invoices to.

Please, note that the date is inclusive, meaning It will include invoices generated on the selected date, too.

Next, select “Generate CSV Download” from the “Tasks” button. Once the CSV file has finished generating, you will see a success message while the file should automatically download locally in the background.

The export then can be saved if needed for later use, in which case click the “Save” button.

Additionally, previous Sage exports can be viewed and have the export files downloaded if needed:

Locate the desired export record from the list.

Once open, select “Generate CSV Download” from the “Tasks” button.

Figure 63 - Creating a Sage export.

Settings

The settings menu is used not necessarily to change the settings for the signed in user but rather to keep & manage systemwide settings in one place – as such, not everyone has permission to access it.

NOTE:

Whether a user can access the “Settings” menu or not is linked to permission levels – this might mean that you will not be able to access it.

A few examples of settings that can be changed:

User settings (name, emails, units they belong to)

Organisation unit’s setup

Documents

Quote related information.

Report Issue & Feedback Form

Although, separate sections within CymBuild, both processes utilise Microsoft Forms – as such, the process of completing these are identical & straightforward. Simply, after opening the links, fill out all the mandatory fields (marked with *) and click submit.

